## Description

When an end-developer uses the `{{container-query}}` modifier in a TypeScript project, they will need to type `dimensions` and/or `features`, i.e. the return values.

<details>

<summary>Example</summary>

```ts
/* app/components/chart.gts */

import { action } from '@ember/object';
import Component from '@glimmer/component';
import { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking';
import type { Dimensions } from 'ember-container-query/modifiers/container-query';
import { containerQuery } from 'ember-container-query';

export default class ChartComponent extends Component {
  @tracked height!: number;
  @tracked width!: number;

  @action updateDimensions({ dimensions }: { dimensions: Dimensions }) {
    const { height, width } = dimensions;

    this.height = height;
    this.width = width;
  }

  // ...

  <template>
    <div {{containerQuery onQuery=this.updateDimensions}}>
      <svg></svg>
    </div>
  </template>
}
```

</details>

[The types have been publicly available since `v2.1.1`](https://github.com/ijlee2/ember-container-query/blob/2.1.1/addon/modifiers/container-query.ts#L7-L25), but the end-developer had to remember the (long) import paths. In this pull request, I re-exported the types in `src/index.ts` so that they can more easily consume the addon's types.

```ts
// Before
import type { Dimensions } from 'ember-container-query/modifiers/container-query';
import { containerQuery } from 'ember-container-query';

// After
import type { Dimensions } from 'ember-container-query';
import { containerQuery } from 'ember-container-query';

// In one line (TypeScript v3.8+)
// https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/modules.html#importing-types
import { containerQuery, type Dimensions } from 'ember-container-query';
```

Note, re-exports can also help us refactor code. As long as the names of the types remain the same, we can move the types to another file to help with file organization, for example. The end-developer won't be affected when they have imported the types from `index.ts`.

